--- a/docs/content/reference/routing-configuration/kubernetes/gateway-api.md
+++ b/docs/content/reference/routing-configuration/kubernetes/gateway-api.md
@@ -628,6 +628,47 @@ For more information on service-level middlewares, see [service middlewares](../
         prefix: /api
     ```
 
+#### Timeouts
+
+An HTTPRoute rule can set timeouts with the `timeouts` field ([GEP-1742](https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/geps/gep-1742/)):
+
+| Field | Traefik behavior |
+|-------|------------------|
+| `request` | Sets the read and write timeouts of the routers created for the rule. The timeout covers the whole request, from the client to the backend and back. |
+| `backendRequest` | Sets `forwardingTimeouts.responseHeaderTimeout` on a ServersTransport for each Kubernetes `Service` backend of the rule. The other forwarding timeouts keep their default values. |
+
+A duration of `0s` disables the timeout.
+
+!!! note "Reading the response body"
+
+    The `backendRequest` timeout stops when the backend sends its response headers. It does not limit how long reading the response body takes.
+
+```yaml
+---
+apiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1
+kind: HTTPRoute
+metadata:
+  name: whoami
+  namespace: default
+spec:
+  parentRefs:
+    - name: traefik
+      sectionName: http
+      kind: Gateway
+
+  hostnames:
+    - whoami.localhost
+
+  rules:
+    - timeouts:
+        request: 10s
+        backendRequest: 5s
+      backendRefs:
+        - name: whoami
+          namespace: default
+          port: 80
+```
+
 ### GRPC
 
 The `GRPCRoute` is an extended resource in the Gateway API specification, designed to define how GRPC traffic should be routed within a Kubernetes cluster. 
